course: dictionary
lesson: 8528
title: Savannah, the grassland
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A savannah is a large, flat land covered in grass, with only a few trees. The context tells you this: «in real life lions live on grassy savannah». Grassy is the clue, because lions need open land with grass to hunt and rest.
explain: Read the whole sentence before you guess. «Cartoons show the lion as king of the jungle, hunting alone while the lionesses rest; in real life lions live on grassy savannah, and the lionesses do most of the hunting, working together.» The word «jungle» is in the cartoon part, and the savannah is in the real-life part. The two are different places.
explain: A capital letter changes the meaning. Savannah with a small s is the grassland. Savannah with a capital S is a girl's name or a city in Georgia, USA. Check the sentence to see which one it is.
fact: A savannah is a large, flat grassy land with few trees.
fact: Savannahs are found in hot places, such as Africa, where zebras and lions live.
fact: A savannah has wet and dry seasons.
fact: On the savannah, a food chain can be grass, then zebra, then lion.
fact: «Savannah» with a capital S is a girl's name or a city in Georgia, USA. «Savanna» is another spelling of the grassland word.
exercise: «In real life lions live on grassy savannah.» What is a savannah? | *A large, flat grassy land with few trees | A deep, dark forest full of tall trees | A river that runs down to the sea | A cold mountain covered in snow
exercise: «In real life lions live on grassy savannah.» Which word is a clue that the savannah is covered in plants? | real | *grassy | lions | live
exercise: Which sentence uses Savannah as a name or a place, not the grassland? | The savannah has few trees. | Lions rest on the savannah in the heat. | *Savannah is a city in Georgia, USA. | Zebras run across the savannah.
test: «The lionesses do most of the hunting, working together.» In real life, who does most of the hunting? | Cartoon kings | *Lionesses | Zebras | Grass
test: Which of these is a food chain you could find on the savannah? | Sea, fish, whale | Snow, bear, seal | *Grass, zebra, lion | Rock, cactus, snake
exam: Why does the capital letter in «Savannah» matter? | It shows a sentence has just started, and nothing more | It shows the grassland is very big | Capital letters make no difference at all | *With a capital letter it can be a name or a city, not the grassland
